  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved governance of labour migration and mobility in line with ILS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO, in partnership with the Caribbean Community (CARICOM) Secretariat and other stakeholders, will provide technical assistance to develop a regional Labour Migration Policy Framework and Action Programme. The initiative will engage governments, employers and workers&#x2019; organizations to promote safe, regular labour mobility, protect migrant workers&#x2019; rights, and strengthen regional integration. It builds on the CARICOM Labour Market Assessment, consultations with social partners and government officials, and regional strategy documents. The process includes preparation of background materials, two rounds of regional consultations, drafting and validation of the policy framework. The work aims to support free movement, rights protection, productive employment, and regional economic integration.</narrative>
  </description>
